  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class C4 (HMO-house in multiple occupation). (PART-RETROSPECTIVE).",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r \rLocation Plan Dated 25.03.2026;\rEXISTING ELEVATIONS, EXISTING AND PROPOSED BLOCK PLAN UGUR - PL02- RE SUB Dated 17.03.2026;\rPROPOSED FLOOR PLAN PROPOSED ROOF PLAN UGUR  - PL03 - RE SUB Dated 17.03.2026;\rDesign and Access Planning Statement;\rSheffield Stand Specification Sheet;\rVelo-Store Cycle Store Specification Sheet;\rFire Statement;\rHighway Safety Impact Form.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r\r",
    "Notwithstanding the approved plans and supporting information, the development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than SIX residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within SIX months from the date of this decision, cycle parking shall be provided on site in compliance with the following criteria:\r\ri) Provision of a minimum of SIX long stay cycle parking spaces\r\rii) In an accessible location; the access route to each long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates [excluding the store door] which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m.\r\riii) Secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob.\r\riv) Fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rSuch facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking.\r",
    "Within SIX months from the date of this decision, details of the design of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. \r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r"
  ],
